  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Inside the surveillance van parked outside the building, Major Lavrov monitors the ongoing sting operation while his handcuffed detainee Pavel grows impatient. Just as tensions peak, Lavrov receives an unexpected phone call from his wife Alla about dinner. Let's listen to the scene in Russian first; don't worry if you don't catch every word right away.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Почему вы просто сидите здесь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Нужно пойти туда и всё прекратить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спокойно, специальная операция продолжается.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Отстегните меня, моя рука затекла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты подождёшь, пока операция идёт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тихо! Мой телефон звонит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Алло, да, Алла Евгеньевна.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, здесь никто не стонет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я скоро буду дома, дорогая.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Овощное рагу на ужин?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, конечно, это прекрасно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "А я могу пойти домой?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Моя жена тоже очень волнуется.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хорошо, идите скорее отсюда.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's walk through the surveillance van scene line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Почему вы просто сидите здесь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why are you just sitting here?' The interrogative adverb opens an impatient question about inaction.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Нужно пойти туда и всё прекратить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We need to go in there and stop everything.' The impersonal predicative modal expresses immediate necessity.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спокойно, специальная операция продолжается.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Calm down, the special operation continues.' The adverb urges patience as the imperfective verb describes an ongoing action.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Отстегните меня, моя рука затекла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Uncuff me, my hand has gone numb.' The imperative verb commands the officer to release the handcuffs.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты подождёшь, пока операция идёт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You will wait while the operation goes on.' The future tense verb indicates required waiting until the task finishes.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тихо! Мой телефон звонит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Quiet! My phone is ringing.' The short imperative calls for silence while the verb indicates an incoming call.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Алло, да, Алла Евгеньевна.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hello, yes, Alla Yevgenyevna.' The standard phone greeting is followed by the formal name and patronymic.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, здесь никто не стонет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, nobody is groaning here.' The negative pronoun pairs with a negated present tense verb.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я скоро буду дома, дорогая.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will be home soon, darling.' The future compound construction indicates planned arrival with an affectionate term.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Овощное рагу на ужин?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vegetable stew for dinner?' The neuter adjective agrees with the noun denoting a domestic meal.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, конечно, это прекрасно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, of course, that sounds wonderful.' The modal particle and short neuter adjective convey enthusiastic agreement.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "А я могу пойти домой?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And can I go home?' The modal predicative combines with a motion verb in a polite request.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "officer",
      "t": "Моя жена тоже очень волнуется.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'My wife is also very worried.' The reflexive verb describes emotional anxiety on the part of the spouse.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хорошо, идите скорее отсюда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Fine, go away from here quickly.' The imperative plural gives permission to depart immediately. Now let's listen to the entire dialogue once again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
